{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded","id":280072,"title":"Why do you like Dragon blooded?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-13T13:48:49-07:00","id":280072,"title":"Why do you like Dragon blooded?","content":"So, it's not really matter for me, cuz my favorite Exalted game line are Lunars. But I like Dragonblooded just becouse they have some willpower.<br /> But why people like Dragonblooded usually?<br /> They are weakest Exalted. They create a quite bad society, and they still fanatically hate other Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T13:58:41-07:00","id":280107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded#post280072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They create a quite bad society</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Was Rome inherently bad? Athens? Imperial China? The French Empire under Napoleon? The British Empire? I could go on.<br /> <br /> Sure, in some ways, all of these were regimes that were truly horrible to certain populations whom they intentionally oppressed, and yet we romanticize them all in other ways.<br /> <br /> The Realm is not an evil nation, or at least not in any way that is unrealistic for an oligarchical imperial power to be. The Realm isn't evil in the way that Mordor is inherently, objectively, metaphysically made of evil. The Realm is evil in the way that human beings with power frequently do evil things for their own betterment. Every great empire commits evil; every great empire justifies evil done to the Other in the name of doing good things for its native citizens. Portraying the major empire of the setting in a manner that downplays the terrible things it does for its own gain and continued hegemony would make the Realm completely unrealistic and unrelatable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T14:09:20-07:00","id":280119,"title":"","content":"I like the Dragon Bloods because they feel like part of the setting, whereas to me, all other Exalt types, either intentionally [Solars] or unintentionally [Lunars] feel like bolt-ons or intentionally buck the synergy of the setting.Being a Dragon Blood means you are part of something which is graspable and thus, feels more immersive. Other Exalt types do power-fantasy better specifically because of their lack of immersion, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T14:10:57-07:00","id":280122,"title":"","content":"First, all the DB aren't living in the Realm.<br /> Second, I like them because they're not perfect. They can impact the setting but not at a young age and without working a lot at it nor without working with a team or family.<br /> I also like them because of the possibility to tell stories of not only one powerfull individual but of an entire family. One of the scenarii I would like to get my players to play, involve a group of post-Contagion survivors, their founding of a kingdom and its developements until present day...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3053,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3053-ikumo","user":"Ikumo","date":". 12-11-2014, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3053-ikumo","name":"Ikumo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T14:21:40-07:00","id":280129,"title":"","content":"The Dragon-Blooded aren't the equal of the Solars, but when confronted with something, they rise to the challenge. A DB game isn't a Solar game, and it shouldn't be treated as one. A DB game works really well when done like a war movie, or a samurai movie, or lower power animes (I don't watch anime very much, so ask someone else about this). Just because they are weaker than a Solar doesn't mean a DB game is a fantastic game. I once ran two simultaneous games of Exalted: Solar group with one Abyssal and Dragon-Blooded group with one Abyssal. In the Solar game they cut a swatch through the Threshold while pursuing their goals, changing every society they visited, making alliances (through brainwashing or other activities). The other game had the same overarching plot line, but the method was much different. Politics wasn't about meeting a few people and using a few Charms. They struck alliances through marriage, political favors. Sometimes they had to assist an army. Some of them died. The Solars gave up and founded their own empire and used the Abyssal as an enforcer. The DBs actually completed the chain of purifying an Abyssal. They had to have other people do a few things, and they paid high prices for it. <br /> <br /> That's kind of what DBs are to me. They are the guys who get the job done. They might not be the lone big damn hero who cuts through the opposition easily, but they are the elite team that gets the job done, even if not everyone makes it.<br /> <br /> Solars are myths. DBs are Seal Team Six.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T14:48:31-07:00","id":280170,"title":"","content":"I like them because of their elemental-aspects, really. Their society and history aren't all that interesting to me - to be honest, their naming conventions is a turn-off to me (I've been struggling with them ever since 1e). I still really love their elemental-flavours and manifestations, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T15:13:33-07:00","id":280189,"title":"","content":"Possiblity for school drama. Hogwarts-if-rated-R/heptagram. Big political drama. Murder investigation that may flip a region. Being a satrap in the time of tumult. Family feuds that date a few generations or 800 years back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T15:40:27-07:00","id":280202,"title":"","content":"What's not to love?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T15:49:47-07:00","id":280207,"title":"","content":"Dragonbloods aren't reeeally my favourite... but they were and when I'm in a Dragonblooded mood:<br /> <br /> I like anything that was created weak and became stronger than it was supposed to be - like, I prefer, in theory, the Enlightened Undercastes of the Mountain Folk to the Artisans' intentional design. Or where the ability of the Sidereals to create the Sidereal Martial Arts wasn't seen or intended by the Maidens, its an unexpected wrinkle in their plan and it may just make everything better (even though they are, gods of foresight). Subverting divine intentions and order. It's about tenaciously rejecting what Heaven tells you is your place and what your life should be, not about having Heaven tell you that you are the one true king.<br /> <br /> (Exalted is designed so all the main splats can be underdogs you root for on one level or another. I really like the divine order subverting one, where the destined king that Heaven sent is not the one who saves the day, other people prefer the one where Solars are just like pulp heroes who rise from anywhere and whose skill and drive is a clear and simple extension of the human in a world of other people who master, understand and turn to human purposes the essence outside the human. And so on.)<br /> <br /> I particularly like that rough edged, wild, natural, unpretentious elemental magic is particularly well suited for the aesthetic of overrunning your purpose - elemental power gets the job done where the fancy, yet somehow hollow magic of the Enlightened Ones doesn't.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of powers and skills that work with uniting their master and his essence more closely with nature, where the master takes on nature's aspect, rather than merely manipulate it. Be water, my friend. (The Lunars' powers also have some of this).<br /> <br /> I like the idea of people who are flawed themselves, and whose personalities are far from all being world shaking and part of a flawed society. I like the idea that many people like this can make real change in the world.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a larger canvas of people working together roughly as equals to change the world than where the broad focus is on a canvas of just less around 1000 (for all that that any game is going to tight focus on a few).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T16:04:26-07:00","id":280210,"title":"","content":"1. Cut-throat Dynastic politics! Other Exalts can get into intrigue, especially Sidereals, but nobody else does politics like a Dynast.<br /> 2. Playing the Underdog. Hunting a dangerous Solar or Lunar as part of a PC Wyld hunt is scary and fun in a way that's harder to get as a more high-powered Exalt.<br /> 3. Because Being Rich Is Awesome. Sometimes you want to play an entitled rich bastard or a spoiled princess and throw your money and your pomposity around. Dynasts do it best.<br /> 4. They've got charms to kill a man from thirty feet away with a sweet guitar riff. I mean sure, so do Abyssals and Infernals, but come on, plucking a string to sever a head is badass.<br /> 5. Elemental superpowers: Look, sometimes you want to go all Poison Ivy or Human Torch or Avatar State Yip Yip on somebody, and Dragonblooded control of the elements is awesome.<br /> 6. Elemental Supersoldier Noir: The Realm is a place of corruption and intrigue and vice...but it's also a place that encourages honor and service in its upper class, and the conflict between the two can make for beautiful stories about well-intentioned young Dynasts struggling to take down corrupt elders or to protect the weak from the heartless bureaucracy or change the system from the inside. Dragonbloods do this best: Solars tend to tear the system down and replace it, Lunars and Sidereals tend to go all uncatchable superhero, but Dragonblooded would-be reformers rarely have the advantage of magical anonymity and thus you get interesting plots as the system tries to stamp them down. Wandering dragonblooded Magistrates appointed by the Empress but now abruptly without any support from their superiors teaming up to make sure they've got each others' backs makes for a FANTASTIC PC Sworn Brotherhood.<br /> 7. School drama: the House of Bells and the Heptagram are bloody brilliant.<br /> 8. The Empty Throne: I wanna outfight Auntie Mnemon and outmaneuver cousin Ejava and win the civil war and bloody well SIT on that shiny five-headed chair. And then I want to deal with the trials and tribulations of running the Empire for a while as the Anathema grow in strength on the borders...<br /> 9. Bein' Prince of the Earth: It's nice being able to wander around being open about what you are and watching mortals bow and scrape before you without worrying about if you're drawing the Wyld Hunt's attention. Playing an elemental Bodhisattva is fun!<br /> 10. The Immaculate Order: Playing devoutly religious characters is sometimes a lot of fun! The Order is pretty well-defined and has lots of fun guidelines for how to live life properly. Trying to maintain your vegetarian lifestyle and keep up your meditation and defend the weak and teach the way of the Dragons while traveling with a party of PCs is tons of fun, and getting your worldview challenged over the course of the game is fun too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T16:31:36-07:00","id":280247,"title":"","content":"The dragon-blooded have both a lower power-level, and greater integration with the setting as a whole, this forces them to work within the world of exalted rather than bulldoze their way over it in the fashion of the celestial exalted. The Celestial Exalted, once they surpass the rookie stage quickly pass <i>several</i> tiers of power above many setting elements, making it difficult to integrate any of that stuff into their stories in a meaningful way.<br /> <br /> Also, the way the setting is structured Dragon-blooded have far more in group variability, especially in terms of life experience. There are really new dragon-blooded and really old ones, and they occupy all possible roles and expressions of exalted power. Solars/Abyssals/Infernals are almost universally new to their power, and while Lunars have a broader dynamic the existing fluff really scatters the group, while sidereals are limited by their small group size (also a problem for Infernals) and specialized duties. The abundance and breadth of the dragon-blooded host allow for roles and possibilities that don't work with celestial exalted (excepting integrated stories, but the inherent enmity the setting designed makes that tricky).<br /> <br /> To me the dragon-blooded just have more possibility (at least within exalted as currently designed) than the other groups. Also I feel the general absence of cheap perfect defenses makes combat descriptively more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T17:23:30-07:00","id":280278,"title":"","content":"I think I would like DB more if I &quot;fixed&quot; some aspects of the setting that bug me, e.g. the Great Cruse, the so-called 'perfection' of the Solar (the Solar Exaltation may be perfect, but grafting a perfect onto a non-perfect does not make a perfect), the idea that the Deathlords are supposed to be a remotely worrying threat. Not meaning to turn this into a 'bagging on Exalted issues' thread, we all know these exist.<br /> <br /> For example, the Great Cruse being a curse laid on the Exalted/Solar, which makes them go bad. If, instead, their madness was the inevitable result of moving further and further away from flawed humanity, then you can view the DB as a kind of 'safety mechanism': from what we saw of the First Age, it's not impossible for a Solar to get it into their head that they should destroy a mountain (and everyone who lives on it) to create a piece of art with the land. When they get that mad, it's the job of the DB to take them down. They'll get mowed down, sure, but enough DB can kill a Solar, even if it's whole armies on one. That would help feed into their military and discipline theme, and also give a better reason for their current anti-Solar vendetta than &quot;the Sids made us do it and we're dumb!&quot; Plus, it'd make the one advantage the DB have over the Solar - the Solars comparatively more difficult dealing with elemental attacks - make a lot more sense.<br /> <br /> Stuff like that. Then all the Exalts would work together a bit more thematically: the Solar may be the great rulers, but the Sids advise them, the Lunar support and guard them (both in the sense that the Solar are protected and the world is protected from them) and the DB as a fail-safe. Would explain why the DB are so battle-oriented and comparatively weaker, too: weaker makes them closer to human, and as such the 'drift' would be lesser.<br /> <br /> Hell, you wouldn't even really need to change the outcome. The DB may have still overthrown the Solar (maybe reasoning the gains weren't worth the losses), but the problem is they just aren't capable of dealing with the issues. Then you're cooking with gas, theme-wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T19:27:11-07:00","id":280422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded#post280072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are weakest Exalted. They create a quite bad society, and they still fanatically hate other Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I like them, basically! I mean, okay, in 2e they were <i>far</i> too weak, but the power level of the dragon-blooded, and the rich social framework they use to supplement it, make them feel much more integrated into the world. Dragon-Blooded are a bit like playing an oWoD Vampire game -- you've got this rich, intrigue-filled society full of complex alliances and backstabbing, and you're accustomed to feeling and thinking of yourselves as being on top of the world, but you're distantly aware that the night is full of vast horrors that dwarf you in power, and so you have a kind of paradoxical position -- larger than life, but not so much so that worldly concerns don't loom large in your world and story.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T19:38:42-07:00","id":280428,"title":"","content":"I liked the idea that the dragonblood were the group that worked best as a team. I mean like every other exalt was technically designed with the idea of it operating as a solo unit. Not to say none of the others could do teamwork or that they didn't benefit from having partners, just that the dragonbloods made sense to me as the group who built upon the others. <br /> <br /> Well that and the way I always explained it to my players the dragonbloods have two main advantages. First other exalts don't really go through their lives expecting the moment they'll become an exalt, the dragonblood are trained with the mindset that all of them will exalt. As a result random guy exalts as a dawn caste and gets combat ability as inheritance from his past life good for him maybe it bolsters his militia training, but just as likely the guy has no military training and isn't more than a brawler. Now he's got to deal with a squad lead by several individuals who were trained long before their bodies were able to bypass their old limits through magic with the idea that they would need to be able to take the best warriors around through brute force.<br /> <br /> The other was more silly, but still valid. &quot;The anathema is bragging about being as powerful as 100 men. Got it we'll see if we can't throw 200 dragonbloods at him. See him laugh then.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T19:48:13-07:00","id":280434,"title":"","content":"I like the Dragonbloods because they can't individually reshape the fate of a whole nation purely by their own innate, individual powers, and yet they are powerful enough to stand on the playing field. I like the Dragonbloods because there are places where they haven't historically been written well, and I can feel the joy of accomplishment as I preach to others about what I will, for roughly a week, consider to be the one true fix to an issue in their depiction. I like the Dragonbloods because they bring stories to the table which scarcely overlap with any other group of Exalts.<br /> <br /> I like the Dragonbloods because I can repeat the words I like the Dragonbloods until they cease to sound like words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T22:58:01-07:00","id":280633,"title":"","content":"I like DBs because combat without spammable perfect defences is far more fun. Because their houses/aspects/schools gives you plenty of combination plot hooks to build a character off. Because it's fun to play a morally ambiguous character who believes themselves to be the good guy and has enough evidence to back it up, even if I the player can see the problems.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T23:17:57-07:00","id":280636,"title":"","content":"I like Dragon Blooded society, as well as the idea of being a Prince of the Earth - being able to go nearly anywhere in Creation and people will bow before you. That's really what makes them feel so different from other Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T23:19:08-07:00","id":280637,"title":"","content":"Elemental power, 'nuf said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T23:39:48-07:00","id":280641,"title":"","content":"I like the dragon blooded because they are the backbone of the exalted. they do all the mundane work and the heavy lifting. they kept civilization from collapsing during the dark times. when the solars became despots and their lunar mates refused to acknoledge their sins, the dragon bloods took it upon themselves to rise up against their former masters and heroes of the primordial war. that can't have been an easy decision.<br /> <br /> And when the armies of chaos came boiling from the wyld to lay waste to form and function as they advanced, it was the dragon bloods who met them upon the field and it was a dragon blooded officer who braved the defenses of the imperial manse to activate it's ancient weapons to drive back the legions of disorder unto the chaos from which they sprang.<br /> <br /> No matter if the terrestrials are fighting off the forces of darkness or engaging in regicide, they always do so with style and panache.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T00:24:31-07:00","id":280665,"title":"","content":"1: They have an established and fairly complex society.<br /> 2: Celestials make for splendid Dragon-Blood antagonists.<br /> 3: Dragon-Blooded don't usually have charms that completly remove one or more ways to challange them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3085-chance","name":"chance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T00:37:02-07:00","id":280684,"title":"","content":"There are a couple of reasons Terrestrials are my favourite host of Exalts in 2e. Remember that this is the perspective of one who has never actually played a Terrestrial, and only ever a handful games of Exalted in any capacity, though.<br /> <br /> They are fun to write Charms for. I always thought Solar Charms were a bit boring to write, because they were often in the vein of &quot;you are immune to this&quot; or &quot;you can parry anything&quot;. Terrestrial Charms (disregarding the elemental imagery which is neat but not essential to me) need to be weaker than that, and the easiest way to do that, besides having smaller numbers, was to restrict when the Charm could be used. Those clauses served as a neat way of forming a statement on the Terrestrials and their society, and made it feel like the powers they used reproduced that society. It made you feel involved in their culture much more than writing for Solars did.<br /> <br /> Naturally, there's a lot to be said against Charms having center stage and that we should focus on characters instead. I that's certainly right, but there's a difference between focusing on characters and making Charms boring or non-thematical. I hope the Terrestrials get to keep their restrictive conditions on their Charms in 3e. They need them to make their society make sense.<br /> <br /> I also like their underdog perspective. It's really strange, because from the start, <i>Solars</i> were supposed to be the underdogs, having just come out of the Jade Prison to suddenly find themselves faced with century-old empire bent on their extermination. I suppose it's a testament to how well 2e represented the value of infrastructure that Solars still came out feeling like the stronger party. In 3e this might change. Instead, Terrestrials kind of feel like hopped-up footsoldiers in the face of their returning general. And well... I kind of like that, actually.<br /> <br /> And I must say I never once heard anyone call a Solar an &quot;underdog&quot;. Sure, there are accounts of Wyld Hunt threatening them, but then it's just a matter of not being strong enough yet and when you are you'll be fine. There's no bloody edge of desperation with Solars. The setting doesn't really let them prove themselves to show their worth, it kind of presents them as inherently worthy and that these people, while currently stronger than you, are actually your lessers and <i>will</i> fall in time. For a Terrestrial, or even a group of Terrestrials, that edge is there. Fighting a Solar is a matter of life and death. The setting does not assure them they will eventually win, in fact it goes to lengths to show why you may not. There are real things at stake here; your life, your friends' lives, maybe even your whole culture. There's defiance in their eyes, which just isn't there in the Solar's.<br /> <br /> To clarify, I've no idea how this feels in actual play. Solars may in fact be proper underdogs. My views are based on how the books and the boards talks about them. A player behind the wheel might help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T03:00:29-07:00","id":280767,"title":"","content":"Dragon Blooded in general: I like extended family politics drama and the idea of an acute martial inclination wrapped up in elemental motifs. It's clean and grounded.<br /> <br /> Scarlet Dynasty in particular: Because I like the attractive aesthetic elements of decadent nobility and social posturing and cutthroat intrigues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T03:10:53-07:00","id":280771,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded are about tradition, and duty, and the glory of working for something greater than yourself- a Realm that is wide and powerful and intriguing and lovely, even as it is crumbling into dust. A lot of character arcs in fantasy are about sticking it to the Man, about being new and unique and- let's face it- more important, somehow, than other people.<br /> I understand why those plots are valid, but sometimes I don't want to read about the village of Berk being changed forever. Sometimes I don't want the heroes to tear down what already exists in pursuit of a Glorious Destiny.<br /> Sometimes I want to read about characters who <i>know</i> the world they live in, not simply explore it or conquer it or remember it from thousands of years ago. Sometimes I want to play as Mulan, and find new ways to honour old responsibilities. Sometimes I want to feel that familial pride, that stability, secondhand.<br /> That's why I like the Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T05:22:28-07:00","id":280894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=280684#post280684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I must say I never once heard anyone call a Solar an &quot;underdog&quot;. Sure, there are accounts of Wyld Hunt threatening them, but then it's just a matter of not being strong enough yet and when you are you'll be fine. There's no bloody edge of desperation with Solars. The setting doesn't really let them prove themselves to show their worth, it kind of presents them as inherently worthy and that these people, while currently stronger than you, are actually your lessers and <i>will</i> fall in time. For a Terrestrial, or even a group of Terrestrials, that edge is there. Fighting a Solar is a matter of life and death. The setting does not assure them they will eventually win, in fact it goes to lengths to show why you may not. There are real things at stake here; your life, your friends' lives, maybe even your whole culture. There's defiance in their eyes, which just isn't there in the Solar's.</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less a perfect description of why I find running Dragon-Blooded a joy compared to Solars and I imagine more or less any Celestial except Sidereals who have their problems.<br /> <br /> Facing down the Wyld Hunt doesn't have the same weight and drama as does surviving and possibly defeating that lone near invincible anathema who spread chaos and threatens everything you stand for not just your life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3085-chance","name":"chance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T06:56:42-07:00","id":280966,"title":"","content":"Above ALL I like Dragonblooded for their Element aspect (no pun intended). Which brings me in conflict with the Immaculate Order always preaching to restrain, to counter your elemental tendencies. I love a Dragonblooded who lets his element run wild and the reason I dislike Dynasts is much because of how self restrained they have to for the Immaculate Order not to be always on top of them or don't lose face before your peers who can use it politically against you.<br /> <br /> I also love Lookshy. The power that defies the Empire, their mix of japanese with spartan society and aesthetics and ascension through merit for DB and Mortal alike.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless I'm having quite some fan playing a DB Dragon Lady from House V'Neef fighting for Ejava in the civil war and going out all fiery war machine despite being a Wood Aspect.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Dragon Styles are made of pure awesome!<br /> <br /> Politics! Those who love political and intrigue games can't get enough of DB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T07:09:12-07:00","id":280974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=280633#post280633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like DBs because combat without spammable perfect defences is far more fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but this shouldn't be a DB-only Thing in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:34:49-07:00","id":281143,"title":"","content":"I like the Dragon-Blooded because of their (intended) mechanics, their setting verisimilitude, and their story potential.<br /> <br /> If Exalted were an MMO, the Dragon-Blooded would be the players and the Celestials would be the raid bosses. I can relate to that premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T03:41:43-07:00","id":282142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=281143#post281143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Dragon-Blooded because of their (intended) mechanics, their setting verisimilitude, and their story potential.<br /> <br /> If Exalted were an MMO, the Dragon-Blooded would be the players and the Celestials would be the raid bosses. I can relate to that premise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> THAT WOULD BE AWESOME. I could totally play that! Empire as one faction, Lookshy as the other, Aspects as races... sorry for the offtopic I got carried away xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T04:18:40-07:00","id":282153,"title":"","content":"I see a lot of reasons why people like Dynasts, which is fine, but nothing specific to Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> I like Dragonblooded because of their thematics of their power. They are Princes of the Earth. Their power either comes from or is inspired by the 5 Terrestrial Dragons and the Pillars of the Elements that keep Creation anchored in reality. Without them, Creation would likely dissipate. They are figuratively the Exalted of Creation.<br /> <br /> Their power is not given down from on high, it is passed by blood and lineage. Strong traditions run with blood. Blood and lineage are very mortal conceits. This grounds them in mortality and the people. This also sets them above people. The power is passed by lineage, which ties you to something strong. Not just anyone can be them, whereas a Solar is chosen from on high, but anyone could be chosen. They are figuratively the Exalted of the People, those Above and Below others.<br /> <br /> Be they Dynasts or Scavenger Lords they are many, they are powerful, they are deeply tied to Creation in a way no other splat is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T07:09:07-07:00","id":282255,"title":"","content":"I guess most of what I like is the elemental affiliation (and how your element should affect your personality and behavioral norms associated with your Aspect); that they are the &quot;underdog Exalted&quot; in that they really have to fight smart and use group tactics to win, being individually less powerful; the opportunities for politics set up by their societies; and that their default setting is &quot;recognized demigod&quot; to pretty much everyone in Creation. They're kind of the Ventrue of Creation and I like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T07:21:59-07:00","id":282271,"title":"","content":"@Godjaw great points made in your post. I agree with your perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T12:04:36-07:00","id":284016,"title":"","content":"I like dragonbloodeds becuase they prove that in Creation team work and tactics matter more then presonal power and ego.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1685-looker","name":"Looker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T02:10:51-07:00","id":285788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=282153#post282153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see a lot of reasons why people like Dynasts, which is fine, but nothing specific to Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> I like Dragonblooded because of their thematics of their power. They are Princes of the Earth. Their power either comes from or is inspired by the 5 Terrestrial Dragons and the Pillars of the Elements that keep Creation anchored in reality. Without them, Creation would likely dissipate. They are figuratively the Exalted of Creation.<br /> <br /> Their power is not given down from on high, it is passed by blood and lineage. Strong traditions run with blood. Blood and lineage are very mortal conceits. This grounds them in mortality and the people. This also sets them above people. The power is passed by lineage, which ties you to something strong. Not just anyone can be them, whereas a Solar is chosen from on high, but anyone could be chosen. They are figuratively the Exalted of the People, those Above and Below others.<br /> <br /> Be they Dynasts or Scavenger Lords they are many, they are powerful, they are deeply tied to Creation in a way no other splat is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, except Sidereals. Amusingly, I always thought about Sidereals as the &quot;Exalts if Creation&quot;, if anything. Their power tends to be about twisting Fate and making the environment not work properly, or about invoking terrestrial spirits and elementals, or just straight up fooling people. Despite being based in heaven, few powersets are as non-selfcontained, which links them to creation maybe not in theme but in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T12:10:42-07:00","id":286102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=285788#post285788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, except Sidereals. Amusingly, I always thought about Sidereals as the &quot;Exalts if Creation&quot;, if anything. Their power tends to be about twisting Fate and making the environment not work properly, or about invoking terrestrial spirits and elementals, or just straight up fooling people. Despite being based in heaven, few powersets are as non-selfcontained, which links them to creation maybe not in theme but in practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, surely the Sidereals are figuratively the Exalted of Heaven. They do the work of Heaven, be it managing Fate and Destiny, policing and deliberating with Gods and Spirits, beings the wardens of the great prison Malfeas, or sages plumbing the depths of the Underworld and it's own twisted Fate.<br /> <br /> Sidereals have always been to me very otherworldly like no other, more akin to the Fair Folk that other Exalted. Once mortal, their company is now of the gods, their game is destiny, their tools are fate. There is a disconnect there in every Sidereal. One can play at being a normal mortal, wear their face and play their game, but mortals are bound by strings they cannot see, whereas Sidereals can see and manipulate them. This thing even divides them from other Exalted. They also were granted the power to directly manipulate fate, but every Exalted is granted mastery of their own, though they cannot manipulate it, they are not bound by it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T14:00:30-07:00","id":286152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Looker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=284016#post284016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like dragonbloodeds becuase they prove that in Creation team work and tactics matter more then presonal power and ego.</div> </div> </div> </div>maybe in 3e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T14:34:45-07:00","id":286181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emeraldstreak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=286152#post286152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> maybe in 3e</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It worked like that in 2e too. Unless your opponent had a DV penalty canceler a lone DB, his mortal archer buddies, a war excellency and a power bow will fuck you right up. Also assuming you don't go first and pop his head right off. Otherwise he'll coordinate his allies, tank the balls off your DV and feather your defenseless ass with a million arrows. It's just that any DV penalty canceler will completely counter the strategy for minimal mote costs. The worst part is that unlike some counter charms almost everybody picks up a penalty canceler at some point due to it being a prerequisite for your PD. It's indicative of some of the problems with exalted. &quot;Here's a cool mechanic! And here's how Solars never have to interact with it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T10:26:57-07:00","id":286744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=286181#post286181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It worked like that in 2e too. Unless your opponent had a DV penalty canceler a lone DB, his mortal archer buddies, a war excellency and a power bow will fuck you right up. Also assuming you don't go first and pop his head right off. Otherwise he'll coordinate his allies, tank the balls off your DV and feather your defenseless ass with a million arrows. It's just that any DV penalty canceler will completely counter the strategy for minimal mote costs. The worst part is that unlike some counter charms almost everybody picks up a penalty canceler at some point due to it being a prerequisite for your PD. It's indicative of some of the problems with exalted. &quot;Here's a cool mechanic! And here's how Solars never have to interact with it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are two angles to why DBs fail to prove teamwork beats ego in 2e.<br /> <br /> The first is that setting-wise the Dynasts (not Lookshy) are exceedingly powered and motivated by egoism. Starting with the Empress, who's the epitome of a solo DB from the moment she got to the Imperial Manse. She made it on her own, she confided in no one, even her fall was so &quot;single&quot; her own children aren't sure what happened. Next is Mnemon, different generation, same story. From the murders in the Heptagram to her solo bid for the throne. Her greatest power? An artifact for her own use, granting her a unique power by DB measures. Sworn Brotherhoods? Never mentioned. Even the lesser, and more protagonist-y, DBs are basically lone wolves. Blackrose, Kes, the Slug...all their triumphs are solo accomplishments, while the pains of their failure are hidden/unconfided.<br /> <br /> Then there's the system-angle. While results differ wildly depending on optimization/circumstances/etc/etc, it's hard to make a case that Solars aren't operating on a level the Realm is simply not equipped to address at all. Compared to the world-altering powers of Solar Sorcery and charms, the Realm, scraping day-by-day on meager tributary taxes and mounting feeble defenses against the threats overwhelming Creation, comes out so pathetic it's not even worth destorying before the God-Kings deal with more pressing matters and establish greater power bases in the Wyld and the Threshold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","user":"emeraldstreak","date":". 10-19-2014, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T11:11:15-07:00","id":286800,"title":"","content":"Infamously, in 2e, the absence of applicability-trumping perfect defenses in the native Dragon-Blooded Charmset means that it is possible for a Solar (and not even all that hard, really) to build a combo that can instantly slaughter every Dragon-Blood within a given radius without possibility of defense on his first action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T11:23:17-07:00","id":286806,"title":"","content":"Hah, yeah, I always liked how the signature DBs not only aren't in a brotherhood, but many actively want to kill the others. Sig Sids are the best in my opinion, all sig circles could stand to take a lesson or two from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T11:31:28-07:00","id":286811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=286806#post286806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hah, yeah, I always liked how the signature DBs not only aren't in a brotherhood, but many actively want to kill the others.[</div> </div> </div> </div>This was a problem with most of the splat sigs written, regardless of splat. Just super duper unpleasant personalities and it's questionable why anyone would ever work with them beyond just needing Super X Magic Power That Only Arianna Or Swan Has.<br /> <br /> Not exactly the best examples for new players to take a note from.<br /> <br /> Now Sids and Alchemicals, I think they did it right. Mainly because their sigs weren't written from the ground up as antisocial assholes. Never did understand why that was a conceit for <i>several</i> splatbooks to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T16:15:51-07:00","id":286981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emeraldstreak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=286744#post286744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are two angles to why DBs fail to prove teamwork beats ego in 2e.<br /> <br /> The first is that setting-wise the Dynasts (not Lookshy) are exceedingly powered and motivated by egoism. Starting with the Empress, who's the epitome of a solo DB from the moment she got to the Imperial Manse. She made it on her own, she confided in no one, even her fall was so &quot;single&quot; her own children aren't sure what happened. Next is Mnemon, different generation, same story. From the murders in the Heptagram to her solo bid for the throne. Her greatest power? An artifact for her own use, granting her a unique power by DB measures. Sworn Brotherhoods? Never mentioned. Even the lesser, and more protagonist-y, DBs are basically lone wolves. Blackrose, Kes, the Slug...all their triumphs are solo accomplishments, while the pains of their failure are hidden/unconfided.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it I don't really see teamwork as in competition with the Dynasts ego driven society actually...<br /> <br /> I know like when we think of teamwork, the first idea that springs to mind is, like the Power Rangers, or the Elite Four from Kill La Kill, and those style of heroes. <br /> <br /> And yeah, OK Dynasts are being pushed away from the sentai thing (Outcastes vary and have more cultural freedom to meet it in a straightforward manner). but think of it this way: <br /> <br /> If the Dragonblooded had flexible skills signature to their personality that had effects that varied depending on how they mixed with allies' signature skills, then how much more interesting would plots to get allies on side for one conspiracy or another be? The intrigue genre there is the closest to the Dynasts' default genre - making their magic work together places all the more importance on bonds, betrayal, politics.<br /> <br /> The Roseblack or Mnemon should totally be cultivating elite lieutenants who work well with together and with her. These people shouldn't necessarily be indispensable or dear to their hearts (Mnemon is rather a cold, hard woman and the Roseblack isn't exactly warm), but there's definitely room for them to have allies and to be careful to pick those who synergise with them, while that's a tool for their own ego and agenda.<br /> <br /> The fact that the RB and those like her aren't written like this, I think is more a failure of writing than how it should be. Partly its because the Caste / Aspect Book format we have encourages characters to talk about themselves as individuals in a certain way - their history growing up, what they think about certain kinds of spirits, etc. - that in many ways fits more for Solars. Honestly, I think for Dragonbloods the Aspect Books were geared to an extent towards showcasing people who were exceptional for their society.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Sworn Brotherhoods shouldn't be super permanent in a way that impedes Dynasts having their own agendas, interests and careers, but whenever a Dragonblood is put into a situation, he should be thinking about who he can recruit and work with, get on side, even if they don't care for the power of friendship, and aware that he's at a disadvantage if he's not, because Dragonbloods I think should be inherently that kind of social (but not necessarily pro-social) Exalted, whose powers run together like the elements. Some of these alliances are heartfelt (they're all Stark-Baratheon stuff) and others are purely for political advantage, and everything between that.<br /> <br /> On another level, I think that ratchet of power for cooperating (even in a purely self interested way) also gives a certain amount of heroism to Dragonbloods like the Slug who are pariahs or those who turn their back on that society - they'd actually be giving up something more meaningful and doing something harder than if Dragonblooded were built to thrive alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T18:22:21-07:00","id":287057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=286800#post286800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infamously, in 2e, the absence of applicability-trumping perfect defenses in the native Dragon-Blooded Charmset means that it is possible for a Solar (and not even all that hard, really) to build a combo that can instantly slaughter every Dragon-Blood within a given radius without possibility of defense on his first action.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're not wrong, nor was DrLoveMonkey above when he mentioned the archers scenario.<br /> <br /> I count myself lucky because I've been able to play Exalted in vastly different groups on both the system and the setting axis. It's enlightening to play the game, with say, people who never read the books. People who don't open a splat and say: <i>oh, look, the Perfect is a mortal with a N/A artifact, the Empress is kindnapped by the Ebon Dragon, and we know what all the evil Deathlords are up to as well! </i><br /> <br /> Meanwhile their polar opposites are the people who are not only knowledgeable of all things Exalted (<i>ok, let's go discuss our supersecret plan at the behemoth's cave where Jupiter stole all secrets, so even Jupiter doesn't know what we're up to) </i>but are also very opinionated exactly on questions like how the Realm represents the evils of imperialism.<br /> <br /> To complicate matters more, there are the attribute+ability pools to represent, ie informing the non-book players of important facts/ideas their characters should know or how much Occult should the character of the player with the Jupiter plan have to be in-character to propose it.<br /> <br /> <br /> When it comes to mechanics, there was the circle content to have 1 dot total of hearthstones/artifacts 60 sessions into a campaign, a fair number of Exalted defeated in tavern brawls, the stressed Solar who was losing a battle in a cellar due to darkness but couldn't remember that Solars are light itself; and then there was the circle who had all the perfects and breakers and magic flurries on the very first session of 2E ever and that wasn't even discussed because it was simply the obvious way of the system.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, when it comes to the fluff, Zelbinnean nailed it that 2E went way overboard with the dark characters, and the &quot;exception&quot; characters to the point we could not say what the original intend of a splat was, Dragonblooded included. When it comes to mechanics the low bar for DBs is, well, a normal mortal+anima for a DB character with zero investment in combat played by a player clueless of the system (with standard WhiteWolf writeups being not much better).<br /> <br /> The upper bar greatly depends on optimization but also the <u>relative</u> place of the Dragonbloods in the pecking order of the crunch. That place was fluid depending on incoming splats, erratas, but also on certain key STs' decisions. Very roughly here are the eras of DB power:<br /> <br /> - Early 2E. Right out of the Core itself Dragonblooded had two standings in the system. How come? Well, the issue was stunts. STs who awarded from nearly no to what is now the official guideline didn't allow enough mote regeneration to recoup perfect use. However, there were STs who awarded (and even advocated) stunts on each and every defense, making mote-tapping a Solar spamming Seven Shadow Evasion a baffling epic quest.<br /> <br /> - Late 2E. While there were a number of developments useful for the Dragonblooded, the advent of tick and action-long perfects, followed by the Dawn Solution and Overdrive left the DBs in a terrible mook-rank position. That was the point when Dragonblooded had to rely on effects out of their native charmset simply to patch glaring holes in their capabilities. Meanwhile, a Solar starting with a tick-long perfect, Joy in Adversity, and a scene-long surprise negator was borderline invincible in normal circumstances right out of the box; while high XP Solars were Sharp Light of Judgement beacons who could ostensibly engage entire Dragonblooded armies solo, and even more jarring, disengage to safety under the most hostile of circumstances.<br /> <br /> - 2.5. This is the version most friendly to Dragonblooded, but probably still below what their relative crunch should be to properly represent their setting place (mind you, Celestial combat superiority is only one way they eclipse the Realm).<br /> <br /> <br /> OK, but what does that mean in actual examples of the high bar of Dragonblooded power and how ST decisions' impact the system? I'll give you two examples of actual DB antagonists used in high-powered campaigns.<br /> <br /> The first one is a (fairly) Early 2E character inspired by the Maiden of Mirthless Smile viewpoint story in the 1E Core, the Hill-Crushing Hero, a fearsome Dragonblooded of unmatched stamina and strength. While the original concept was an Outcaste mercenary, this one is an even more deadly Elder Immaculate Grandmaster. The creation date is probably shortly after Scroll of Heroes. The character relies on various adders and multipliers to compensate for the Celestial perfection via straight out-statting them. Mind you, he isn't a match for Late 2E Solars which underlines how the game changed in the 2.0 itself.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">(warning: Merits rage trigger)</span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/MM4FDfC.png\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Earth Grandmaster</span></a></span><br /> <br /> <br /> The next character is one who spearheaded the Usurpation itself, now returning to haunt the Lawgivers more powerful than ever. She was created as a story arc final antagonist (under the last 2.0 errata) for 1,000 XP Solar circle. Yup, facing an entire circle, each Solar at 1k XP with backgrounds to boot. However, this campaign had <b>a major houserule: </b>no mote or Willpower regeneration when one has used a perfect defense, for the duration of said perfect defense only. It was implemented to combat infinite perfect spamming, however, as everything else in the Second Edition it could only improve the flow of the game so far before causing problems of its own. In essence, this houserule shifted the metagame to finding ways to remove unblockable or undodgeable qualities of attacks and negating them with high DVs to gain stunt and charm mote/WP recovery. Of course, there were a number of other RAW clarifications and houserules.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for the example, this character is also an Akuma, but nonetheless showcases the final 2.0 Dragonblooded power. A pure Dragon-Blooded would have 1 dot lower basic stats and would have to use Blade of the Battle Maiden instead of Yozi Inevitability. As I have only a quick combat reference sheet left, let me go over her powers:<br /> <br /> - Mantle of Elemental Fusion, fused with a Lesser Earth Dragon of the Quicksilver Queen stature. The main benefits derived are Essence Plethoras, Destiny Sponsorship inflicted 15 external penalty on attacks against Dodge DV, Invincible Symbol of Authority:Earth that denies/reduces earth and metal based attacks, including magic materials based on metals.<br /> - Transcendant Gaian Harmony:Air and Wood, inflicting 8 to 16 external penalties on certain attacks per the animas (She's Earth Aspect)<br /> - lesser penalty applicators like Consuming Might of the Fire Dragon and Flowing Water Defense (note that her stats presume a fight going on for some time so she has accumulated enough Water Style free motes)<br /> - Unchain the Dragon's Heart: probably won't come into play, but if it does it's a nasty surprise<br /> - Ordained Talons of Draconic Fury on the Eye of the Fire Dragon. That's the Rate 13 weapon line and the artifact itself does aggravated damage and charmbreaks Solars<br /> - a number of renamed hearthstones which (I guess) represent Jewel of the Flying Heart, White Jade Tree, and Gemstone of Shadows<br /> - Crystal Chameleon Speed: for Surprise/Stealth. Note that Flowing Kata allows moving between Forms as needed<br /> - Joy in Adversity. Yeah. The big mote regenerator available to CMA-mooks to even out the field against Solars a bit<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(warning: Cobra rage trigger)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Dragon-Blooded natively lack in many areas that can be addressed by Celestial Martial Arts; at the time Cobra Style offered 1) perfects 2) reflexive attacks, while the major houserule made the root charm of the style better<br /> - since that's just a reference sheet, not a full build, there are many charms not shown, ie the Style Forms under the Flowing Kata. Something interesting not shown is the TMA Smoke Adept Gesture for acting on tick 0. Anyway, <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/xef2thI.png\" target=\"_blank\">here it is</a>.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T04:34:23-07:00","id":287448,"title":"","content":"I'm currently running a 500xp E5 Dragon-Blood alongside a mixed Celestial circle of the same level in a Modern game.<br /> <br /> Despite having zero martial arts Charms, it's working out surprisingly well so far. I think it would be fair to call her one of the group's heaviest hitters. Lack of non-Shaping keyword defences and unconditional surprise negators may yet prove fatal, but <i>damn</i> is Dragon Vortex a versatile and powerful Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T04:59:55-07:00","id":287478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Looker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=284016#post284016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like dragonbloodeds becuase they prove that in Creation team work and tactics matter more then presonal power and ego.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any game involving more than one player will probably do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T05:38:34-07:00","id":287505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=287478#post287478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any game involving more than one player will probably do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah seriously, why do people think that working together is something special that only DB can do anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T06:00:54-07:00","id":287514,"title":"","content":"I just think Fire Aspects are hot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T09:37:51-07:00","id":288630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=287505#post287505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah seriously, why do people think that working together is something special that only DB can do anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because they have so many Charms that benefit from it.<br /> <br /> I've never seen anyone use the Mass Combat system but the DB War suite and their wealth of Leader keyword Charms makes them the pretty clear front runners in that field.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 10-21-2014, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T10:24:59-07:00","id":288667,"title":"","content":"I like them because I feel that they encompass &quot;Doing the Impossible&quot; far more than a Solar ever could. For a Solar, nothing IS impossible or even - after a certain point - all that difficult. Terrestrials are faced with far more challenges with less power, and they face them anyway. After the Usurpation, Terrestrials held the world together. They messed up a lot, sometimes even outright lost, but they did it. When the Contagion swept across Creation and Heaven itself recoiled in terror, the Terrestrials maintained order and tried to cure what could not be cured. When the Balorian Crusade threatened to consume all of Reality, it was the Terrestrials who fought them back. Battling unending hordes of nightmares, against which there was no hope or chance, the Terrestrials fought tooth and nail for every bloody inch of Creation that was lost. Even knowing that there could be no victory, they fought until one of their own did one more impossible thing in a long list of impossible things and took control of a weapon noone alive could safely weild, and ended the endless swarms of the wyld.<br /> They are flawed. They are weak. They are decadent, exploitative, petty, tyrannical and bound by dogma. They are also the true guardians of Creation. They are the ones you can count on to save the day, when nobody else can or will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/776-saintedphysician","name":"SaintedPhysician","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T12:46:04-07:00","id":288801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=287505#post287505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah seriously, why do people think that working together is something special that only DB can do anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it doesn't help that the Solar examples and the text in general tends to point towards Solars having to be generally the kind of people who honestly can only be conceived as working together because of enormous need or plain OOC conceit.<br /> <br /> As for why I like Dragonblooded, well, I think part of it is my liking for family themes (I'm one of those people whose characters actually <i>have </i>parents they are in good relations with), and the other part is their underdog status. I came into the game in 2E, and the general assumption by everyone always seemed to be that the Realm is <i>absolutely boned</i> and the Solars are going to knock it down like a sand castle the moment any of them bother, and there's nothing the Dynasty can do. It's very hard to not feel a pang of sympathy for the guys relegated to props by the unstoppable invincible protagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 10-21-2014, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T01:56:49-07:00","id":289380,"title":"","content":"Being the underdogs is definitely appealing. Along those lines, it feels like you really achieve something when you save the day.<br /> If your Solar PC kills a DB, whatever.<br /> If your DB kills a Solar, it's totally awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T02:30:06-07:00","id":289385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=289380#post289380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being the underdogs is definitely appealing. Along those lines, it feels like you really achieve something when you save the day.<br /> If your Solar PC kills a DB, whatever.<br /> If your DB kills a Solar, it's totally awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping against hope that next edition you'll be able to get that kind of thing out of a Solar. Killing a roving army of Raksha and terrible tainted wyld beasts shouldn't just be going through the motions of activating Infinite Melee Mastery and trollfacing. Then again that kind of thing could even happen with DBs with things like Dragon Vortex Attack, it's just more common with the ultimate badasses that are the Celestial Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T07:49:49-07:00","id":289584,"title":"","content":"Dragon Vortex is one of those charms that suddenly pushes your character to an entirely new and very different level of power. One moment you're a pretty good general who can give minor magical buffs to your troops, next you shoot nukes out of your head and don't even need an army. It's quite a dramatic change.<br /> <br /> But yeah, sometimes with a Solar things just seem too easy. It's why I'm a bit pleased that they're going to reduce the power level of Solars. I like the fact that they can do big dramatic things, but that doesn't mean I want dramatic fights against gods or demons to be so easy the ST thinks maybe he should just say you auto-win to avoid having to go through all the dice rolling.<br /> With DBs, that's rarely an issue, except maybe against mortal extras (who are at least, mechanically, designed to go down quickly).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T15:55:46-07:00","id":290076,"title":"","content":"Re: teamwork and cooperation (or sorts) and the Dragonblooded vs Solars (and others)... <br /> <br /> When I think of people who distinguish themselves and lift themselves up through their willingness to stand out beyond the human norm, to be champions and leaders beyond the norm, I don't really think of people who really *need* to work together and for who mutual support is really important.<br /> <br /> I mean, clearly champions and paragons and people who are above the norm *could* achieve more through teamwork than they could without it (although maybe they'd get on better alone as well - it's not like some people don't). And no man is an island, etc.<br /> <br /> Cooperation just isn't what I would think of for them compared to a group of people whose motif is fundamental primal matter which must come together to create all the complex and wonderful nature which exists in our world. And I wouldn't expect people whose nature is being champions and paragons to have magic as dedicated to it as people whose motifs are being like the elements and being plebian amongst the Exalted.<br /> <br /> (And yes Solars probably should be able to have people amongst them whose mythic special, &quot;lifts me up above the norm&quot;, paragon and champion talent *is* their ability to cooperate and be part of a team, it's not really what binds them together as a splat in the same way. Its a direction they can take, not essentially part of Solar-ness.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T16:33:48-07:00","id":290095,"title":"","content":"I see Solars as being able to team up, and DBs requiring to team up. A group of Solars is like the Avengers or the Justice League, individually heroes of great power and together an unstoppable force. DBs are more like the Guardians of the Galaxy or the Power Rangers. Individually they're not weak, but they have big holes in their personalities and capabilities that they can cover for each other and be way way more effective as a team.<br /> <br /> Basically five Solars is equal to the sum of their parts, basically, but that sum is FUCKING impressive. DBs are greater than the sum of their parts, much greater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T16:34:42-07:00","id":290096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never seen anyone use the Mass Combat system but the DB War suite and their wealth of Leader keyword Charms makes them the pretty clear front runners in that field.</div> </div> </div> </div> Being an effective military commander doesn't seem to be the thing most people are talking about when the subject comes up; more of a super sentai or Captain Planet kind of thing. Personally, my interest is picqued less by the idea that they all provide bonuses to one another or stack up elemental effects, and more in the gameplay and setting implications of how their family and military structures implicitly assume large-scale cooperation between large numbers of them. Mnemon doesn't need a brotherhood shoring up her low stats when she's got her descendents and subordinate allies in a complex organic structure that she can coordinate; a theme of the elements might touch off of that, but it's mostly its own thing. I do find it off-putting when it's framed in terms of &quot;teamwork, yay&quot; triumphalism, mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T16:45:40-07:00","id":290101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=290096#post290096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I do find it off-putting when it's framed in terms of &amp;quot;teamwork, yay&amp;quot; triumphalism, mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about &quot;teamwork, without it we don't stand a chance.&quot;? <br /> <br /> It also works way way the hell better then the DBs are the NPCs. I tried to run a DB game one time and I even gave everyone free artifacts which made all teamwork related charms cost half motes and still nobody used any. Except one person near the end after some more prodding.<br /> <br /> On the flip side I put together an antagonist team of DBs who very nearly killed a circle of celestial exalts because they were all boosting each others soak into the 40s and defending for one another when one started getting whittled down. Lesson learned being that most players will loath the idea of spending 14 motes to super boost their entire party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T17:12:40-07:00","id":290113,"title":"","content":"Large scale coordination is important, but I would say I definitely don't see Dragonblooded, particularly, in terms where they are defined by elders exploiting and managing their descendents, or terms where individual Dragonblooded are cogs in a dehumanising machine, or terms where they are the military soldier Exalted in ways in which the Solars are not generals or war heroes, Sidereals are just military tactians, etc. For all that their society has flaws.<br /> <br /> I'd might say I'd emphasise that Dragonblooded cooperation (for better and worse) is much more about effective personal relationships than impersonal or strongly authority structured relationships. Whether or not those personal relationships are actually what we'd call friendly or warm or altruistic or not. I think that's generally more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T01:50:41-07:00","id":290375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded?p=290113#post290113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd might say I'd emphasise that Dragonblooded cooperation (for better and worse) is much more about effective personal relationships than impersonal or strongly authority structured relationships. Whether or not those personal relationships are actually what we'd call friendly or warm or altruistic or not. I think that's generally more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a distinction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T09:12:57-07:00","id":290541,"title":"","content":"There is, in that most commanders don't know the names of every foot soldier and most foot soldiers don't know the names of everyone higher on the chain of command. While you'll see Dragonblooded who don't know each other helping each other to ward off or slay an Anathema who suddenly Exalts in the same room as them, more often when Dragonblooded are really cooperating it should be with people that they share a certain level of kinship with beyond simply both being Dragonblooded or even just both of the same House, even if the form that relationship takes isn't necessarily what we'd call friendship.<br /> <br /> It's part of why Dynasty Charms were problematic, basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T09:29:17-07:00","id":290564,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking more about the idea that, at least within the Scarlet Dynasty, there's a certain balancing act between maintaining bonds of personal loyalty from child to parent, and having an awareness of their abilities and accomplishments and proclivities, while also maintaining a stoic patrician stand-offishness and clear lines of hierarchy. Not so much impersonal as often aloof, and where jockeying for power with fairly concrete and pervasive people is a frequent thing.<br /> <br /> When I think about how the numbers and nature of the Dragon Blooded lead them to cooperative action, I don't think so much of Planateer-type groupings, nor of a big impersonal machine that diffuses the individual, I think about how, if you're a Terrestrial and you need some Terrestrial magic type action taking place in any major city in the country, it's actually possible for there to be some there. Or for the idea that when some big technical project is going on, you can have a large pool of colleagues and peers to all concentrate in one space for it. It's like... because I've been watching The Good Wife lately, I want to say it's like having high-powered lawyers; between their career paths and their education background, a lot of them will have extensive personal relationships with one another that make for various sorts of coordinated activity.<br /> <br /> It's a thing, and a thing of relevance, but I don't quite think needs to be a thing in their Charms. It's an emergent property.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T18:40:57-07:00","id":290931,"title":"","content":"For me Dragon Blooded seemed the most 'human' of all the Exalts. For all their power they are primal, selfish, and very well, flawed. But they are still heroic and brave. They fit the classic flawed hero mold sometimes better than Solars or other Exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1472-mostlyjoe","name":"Mostlyjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}